# CVE-2026-81521: go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2 — a caller-supplied database
# name in Client.BulkWrite isn't escaped before building the target namespace.
# This server never talks to MongoDB (Postgres/TimescaleDB only, per
# CLAUDE.md) — the driver is an indirect dependency pulled in only for its
# bson sub-package, which gin/binding links in for optional BSON request
# binding (`go mod why -m go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2` confirms the only
# path in is gin -> gin/binding -> mongo-driver/v2/bson). The vulnerable
# mongo.Client.BulkWrite API lives in a different sub-package that is never
# imported, so it is never linked into the binary.
CVE-2026-81521
